{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1766892,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Seek the Civil Geek","festival_id":519255,"organization_id":13183,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-07T00:15:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-11T11:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/seek-the-civil-geek-indian-institute-of-technology-indian-school-of-mines-iit-ism-dhanbad-1766892","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Seek the Civil Geek<\/strong> is a Civil Engineering case-study competition that challenges participants to analyze real-world engineering problems, develop innovative solutions, and present their ideas before a distinguished panel of judges.<\/p>\n<p>The competition provides participants with an opportunity to apply their technical knowledge, analytical thinking, creativity, research skills, and problem-solving abilities to contemporary challenges in Civil Engineering and infrastructure.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Case Study Presentation | Ppt Round<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Shortlisted teams will be provided with a <strong>real-world Civil Engineering case study<\/strong> and will be required to analyze the problem, conduct relevant research, and develop a practical and innovative solution.<\/p>\n<p>The presentation should demonstrate a clear understanding of the problem, the proposed methodology, and the feasibility and impact of the solution.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Participants may encounter challenges related to:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Slope Stabilization &amp; Landslide Management<\/li>\n<li>Green Building Practices<\/li>\n<li>Sustainable Transportation &amp; Smart Mobility<\/li>\n<li>Seismic Resilience<\/li>\n<li>Sustainable Construction Materials<\/li>\n<li>Future-Ready Urban Infrastructure<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Teams are encouraged to consider:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technology Integration &ndash; Emerging technologies and innovative engineering methods.<\/li>\n<li>Social &amp; Economic Impact &ndash; Affordability, inclusivity, employment, and social equity.<\/li>\n<li>Policy &amp; Regulatory Frameworks &ndash; Legal, ethical, and governance considerations.<\/li>\n<li>User-Centric Design &ndash; Safety, accessibility, sustainability, and human needs.<\/li>\n<li>Funding &amp; Financing Models &ndash; Innovative approaches such as Public-Private Partnerships (PPPs).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Presentation Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each presentation must consist of 7&ndash;15 slides.<\/li>\n<li>Teams may use any software to create their presentation.<\/li>\n<li>A Q&amp;A session will follow each presentation.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must clearly communicate their analysis, proposed solution, feasibility, and expected impact.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Content Understanding &ndash; Depth of analysis and clarity of problem comprehension.<\/li>\n<li>Creativity &ndash; Innovation and originality of the proposed solution.<\/li>\n<li>Presentation Quality &ndash; Clarity, structure, visual quality, and professionalism.<\/li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Performance &ndash; Ability to confidently address questions and defend the proposed solution.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Conclusion<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Seek the Civil Geek<\/strong> invites Participants to Think Beyond Conventional Engineering Solutions and Tackle the Multifaceted Challenges Shaping the Future of Infrastructure.<\/p>\n<p>Through Critical Thinking, Research, and Innovation, Participants Will Work Toward Solutions that Promote <strong>Sustainable, Resilient, Technologically Advanced, and Inclusive Infrastructure<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Think. Solve. Build.<\/strong><br \/><strong>Are you ready to Seek the Civil Geek?<\/strong><\/p>","overall_prizes":"Goodies Prizes Worth 7.5k","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":19125227,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"cre